 "nodes": [
  {
   "extras": {
    "edit_note": "A mission building (blender/tools/build_interior_blends.py, seed blender/tools/interior_plans.py): a PLACEHOLDER shell and fit-out at its real Japanese size -- remodel freely. Keep the frame (origin = plot centre on the ground, street -Y), the floor levels, and move the Empties with what they belong to: DOOR_ (interior door, arrow OUT of the room), EXIT_ (outer door, arrow out of the building), LIFT_ (a lift: shaft floor centre at the low stop; stops / faces), MARK_ (a mission marker: kind weapon / spawn / cover ...). Keep 1.2 m clear both sides of every door. After editing: tools/building_kit/build_buildings.sh. \u90f5\u4fbf\u5c40 (main, \u96c6\u914d\u5c40): a three-storey 36 x 26 m post office -- F1 the \u98a8\u9664\u5ba4, the customer hall (\u8a18\u8f09\u53f0, sofas, ticket machine), the \u7a93\u53e3 counters (\u90f5\u4fbf / \u8caf\u91d1 / \u4fdd\u967a) and the \u3086\u3046\u30d1\u30c3\u30af parcel counter, the \u3086\u3046\u3061\u3087 ATM corner, restrooms, the office strip with the safes, and behind it the delivery depot (\u533a\u5206 sorting tables, roll cages) with two dock shutters onto the van yard; F2 offices, the postmaster, a meeting table; F3 offices, the server room, lockers, the canteen. Two stairs (B to the roof), a lift; the red band, the \u3012 board, two red \u30dd\u30b9\u30c8; the van yard behind the docks (a POT-1 box truck, two POV-1 vans)."
   },
